<template><main class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-5 py-12"><RouterLink to="/" class="text-sm font-medium">← Mirror</RouterLink><h1 class="mt-10 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy for try-on photos</h1><div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-sm leading-7 text-muted"><p>Mirror processes photos you explicitly upload to create virtual try-on images and personalized fashion recommendations.</p><p>Shopper photos and generated results are designed to be stored privately and accessed through time-limited signed URLs. Merchant users should not receive unrestricted access to raw shopper photos.</p><p>Your latest uploaded photo becomes the base photo for the current store in this browser. Mirror restores it through your validated fitting session, and you can replace or remove it from Photo settings at any time.</p><p>Mirror should not use shopper photos to train models unless the shopper separately gives explicit permission for that purpose.</p><p>You can remove the current photo from your session. Production deployments should also expose deletion controls for stored source and generated images and define a short retention period appropriate to the pilot.</p><p>Virtual try-ons are visual approximations and are not guarantees of garment sizing, fit, colour accuracy or material behaviour.</p></div></main></template>
